  "id": "exchange-gamecenter-silent",
  "description": "Game Center sign-in with nothing to ask (WIRE-CONTRACT-V5 §12.11.7). The app checks that the local player is already authenticated, so it never presents the Game Center view at launch. exchange() posts the device's keys for a nonce, then takes the player's identity-verification signature from Game Center (public key URL, signature, salt, timestamp in milliseconds, team player id, bundle id) and sends the gc1. token: six dot-joined fields, every one base64url except the decimal timestamp. The grant is the usual form with subject_token_type urn:polaris-key:token-type:gamecenter-signature and the exchange proof over the nonce, the key and the token's hash. The Worker checks the certificate chain, the signature and the window, and finds the team player linked under the developer's team with consent already given: the answer is a device token. The Worker's call to Apple's key host is not part of this conversation.",
